/* book exam traps: A common wavelength on each pair of neighbouring links is not enough. The same wavelength must be free on every link of the path. | A WSS switches a wavelength to another port; it does not change it. Only a wavelength converter turns λ2 into λ3. | Without converters an OXC is W small F × F switches (W × F² crosspoints), not one big FW × FW switch. For 4 fibers and 8 wavelengths that is 128, not 1024. | Splitter losses in dB add: a 1:16 splitter costs 10 log₁₀ 16 = 12.04 dB, and a 16:1 combiner costs another 12.04 dB. | OADM and OXC are not the same: an OADM adds and drops a few local wavelengths on one fiber line, while an OXC can switch any wavelength between many fibers. */
