/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - The Open Systems Interconnection (OSI) model has seven layers.
   - The PDU is a bit at the physical layer, a frame at the data link layer, a packet at the network layer, a segment at the transport layer for TCP (a datagram for UDP) and a message at the application layer.
   - IP can ride on SONET/SDH, on Ethernet, or straight on WDM lightpaths (WDM networks).
   - ATM sends everything in cells of 53 bytes: a 5-byte header and a 48-byte payload.
   - ATM has three layers.
   - Service classes give quality of service (QoS).
   - ATM lost to IP and Ethernet.
*/
