/* book exam traps: Count the 5-byte header: a 48-byte payload costs 53 bytes on the link, not 48. | Add the 8-byte AAL5 trailer before dividing by 48: a 90-byte packet seems to need ⌈90/48⌉ = 2 cells, but 90 + 8 = 98 bytes need 3. | AAL5 pads first and puts the trailer last, in the final 8 bytes of the last cell; the trailer is not between data and pad. | VPI names the path and VCI the channel inside it; do not swap them. AAL1 carries constant-bit-rate voice and AAL5 carries data. | The transport PDU is a segment for TCP but a datagram for UDP; a frame belongs to the data link layer. */
